X11 frames client: exit when the compositor is gone; take frames only
from our own frames client.

mutter stops mutter-x11-frames with SIGTERM when it exits cleanly
(meta_x11_display dispose). After a gnome-shell crash nothing stops it:
there is no PR_SET_PDEATHSIG on illumos. The orphan (ppid 1) keeps
watching _MUTTER_NEEDS_FRAME and frames the new compositor's windows too,
and the MapRequest handler takes any window with _MUTTER_FRAME_FOR as the
frame. On the MacBook Pro (2026-11-20) new windows got the orphan's frames
(their _NET_WM_PID was the orphan's): no resize borders, and clicks raised
the window below.

1. src/frames/main.c: remember the parent pid; exit once getppid ()
   changes (checked every second).
2. src/x11/events.c: take a _MUTTER_FRAME_FOR window as a frame only if
   its _NET_WM_PID is our frames client's pid (GTK sets _NET_WM_PID on
   the frame toplevels); otherwise ignore it.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter (not reported yet).

